=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
The network is fully operational. The helpdesk report that router16 has
"crashed and stopped forwarding" is factually incorrect — direct inspection
shows no fault on any device.

Router16 is alive and healthy: its bond0 uplink (eth0+eth1, 10.2.2.1/24) to
mswitch0 is UP, its WAN-side eth2 (172.30.1.1/24) toward router7 is UP, and
OSPF is running with two Full-state adjacencies — Full/Backup with mswitch0
and Full/DR with router7. The FRR routing table on router16 correctly shows
172.16.10.0/24, 172.16.20.0/24, and 172.16.30.0/24 learned via OSPF from
mswitch0 (10.2.2.2), and these routes are in turn propagated through router7
to the rest of the network.

End-to-end data-plane tests confirm full bidirectional reachability: pc5
(172.16.10.5) reaches its Campus 1 gateway (172.16.10.254 on mswitch0) and
router7's eth4 (172.30.1.2) with 0% packet loss; conversely, router7
successfully pings pc5, the VLAN 20 gateway (172.16.20.254), and the VLAN 30
gateway (172.16.30.254), all with 0% loss.

Root cause: There is no fault. The ticket premise — that router16 has died and
Campus 1 is isolated — is incorrect; the router is forwarding normally and
Campus 1 subnets are fully reachable from the rest of the network.

Corrective action: No change needed. Close the ticket as a false alarm and
advise the reporter to retest connectivity; their original observation does not
match the current (and apparently stable) network state.
=== END ===
